{
  "id": "pc-vectors",
  "chapterNumber": "4",
  "title": {
    "en": "Vectors & Parametric Equations",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A vector has both magnitude and direction. Vectors model force, velocity, and displacement. Parametric equations describe motion and curves by expressing both coordinates as functions of a parameter \\(t\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Vector fundamentals",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>For \\(\\mathbf{u}=\\langle u_1,u_2\\rangle\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}=\\langle v_1,v_2\\rangle\\), scalar \\(k\\):</p>\\[\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v}=\\langle u_1+v_1,u_2+v_2\\rangle,\\quad k\\mathbf{u}=\\langle ku_1,ku_2\\rangle,\\]\\[|\\mathbf{u}|=\\sqrt{u_1^2+u_2^2},\\quad\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}=\\frac{\\mathbf{u}}{|\\mathbf{u}|}\\quad(\\text{unit vector}).\\]<p><strong>Component form from magnitude/angle:</strong> \\(\\mathbf{v}=\\langle|\\mathbf{v}|\\cos\\theta,\\;|\\mathbf{v}|\\sin\\theta\\rangle.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Dot product & angle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=u_1v_1+u_2v_2=|\\mathbf{u}||\\mathbf{v}|\\cos\\theta.\\]<p><strong>Perpendicular:</strong> \\(\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=0.\\quad\\) <strong>Parallel:</strong> \\(\\mathbf{v}=k\\mathbf{u}.\\)</p><p><strong>Vector projection of \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) onto \\(\\mathbf{v}\\):</strong></p>\\[\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{v}}\\mathbf{u}=\\frac{\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}}{|\\mathbf{v}|^2}\\,\\mathbf{v},\\qquad\\text{scalar projection}=\\frac{\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}}{|\\mathbf{v}|}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Parametric equations & eliminating the parameter",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Curve: \\(x=f(t),\\;y=g(t).\\)</p><p><strong>Method 1:</strong> solve for \\(t\\) from one equation, substitute into the other.</p><p><strong>Method 2 (trig):</strong> if \\(x=a\\cos t\\) and \\(y=b\\sin t\\), use \\(\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t=1\\Rightarrow\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\\)</p><p><strong>Projectile motion:</strong> \\(x=v_0\\cos\\alpha\\cdot t,\\quad y=v_0\\sin\\alpha\\cdot t-\\tfrac{1}{2}g t^2.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 4.1 — Dot product and angle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Find the angle between \\(\\mathbf{u}=\\langle4,-3\\rangle\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}=\\langle2,5\\rangle\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>\\(\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=4(2)+(-3)(5)=8-15=-7.\\)</p><p>\\(|\\mathbf{u}|=\\sqrt{16+9}=5,\\quad|\\mathbf{v}|=\\sqrt{4+25}=\\sqrt{29}.\\)</p><p>\\(\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{-7}{5\\sqrt{29}}\\approx\\dfrac{-7}{26.93}\\approx-0.260.\\quad\\theta\\approx105.1°.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 4.2 — Projection",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Project \\(\\mathbf{u}=\\langle6,2\\rangle\\) onto \\(\\mathbf{v}=\\langle3,4\\rangle\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>\\(\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=18+8=26.\\quad|\\mathbf{v}|^2=9+16=25.\\)</p><p>\\(\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{v}}\\mathbf{u}=\\dfrac{26}{25}\\langle3,4\\rangle=\\left\\langle\\dfrac{78}{25},\\dfrac{104}{25}\\right\\rangle.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 4.3 — Eliminate parameter",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Convert \\(x=3\\cos t,\\;y=5\\sin t,\\;t\\in[0,2\\pi]\\) to Cartesian form.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>\\(\\dfrac{x}{3}=\\cos t,\\quad\\dfrac{y}{5}=\\sin t.\\quad\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t=1\\Rightarrow\\dfrac{x^2}{9}+\\dfrac{y^2}{25}=1.\\)</p><p>An ellipse with semi-axes \\(a=5\\) (vertical), \\(b=3\\) (horizontal).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 4.4 — Projectile",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "A ball is kicked at 20 m/s at 60° to the horizontal. Find: (a) max height, (b) range, (c) time of flight.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>\\(v_x=20\\cos60°=10\\text{ m/s},\\quad v_y=20\\sin60°=10\\sqrt3\\text{ m/s}.\\)</p><p>(a) At max height \\(v_y=0\\): \\(t_{\\text{top}}=10\\sqrt3/9.8\\approx1.77\\text{ s}.\\quad H=10\\sqrt3(1.77)-\\frac12(9.8)(1.77)^2\\approx15.3\\text{ m}.\\)</p><p>(b) Time of flight: \\(T=2t_{\\text{top}}\\approx3.53\\text{ s}.\\quad\\text{Range}=10(3.53)\\approx35.3\\text{ m}.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
